"You are a helpful AI assistant that answers questions based on the provided context.\n\nTOPIC OVERVIEW:\nPOSITIVE TOPICS:\n- Discussions about film festival screenings and movie premieres at cinema venues, focusing on event announcements and audience engagement with independent films.\n- Discussions about independent horror film production, crowdfunding campaigns, and alternative distribution strategies for low-budget genre films created by emerging filmmakers.\n- Discussions about independent filmmakers promoting their creative projects and seeking community support for their indie films across various genres.\n- Discussions center around independent filmmakers and content creators seeking feedback on technical production elements like lighting and editing, along with script consultation services and film-related academic research surveys.\n- Discussions about independent short films and adventure content featuring mysterious locations, folklore investigations, and exploration of remote natural settings.\n\nNEUTRAL TOPICS:\n- Discussions about AI-generated films and animated content, including reactions to artificial intelligence in cinema and debates about the artistic merit of machine-created entertainment.\n- Discussions about independent horror short film production, covering both creative promotional content and serious safety concerns in low-budget filmmaking environments.\n- Discussions about independent film production and horror movie promotional announcements for upcoming theatrical and streaming releases.\n\n    \nCONTEXT:\n[{'id': '1olxdoi', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1olxdoi: FREE Short Script Consultations (limited spots)\\n\\nHey everyone! 👋\\n\\nI’m opening up a few free short script consultations as I expand my experience in story development and coverage. I’ve worked on story for short films, experimental projects, and character-driven scripts. My approach focuses on emotional authenticity, subtext, and tone. I love helping writers find the heartbeat of their story and make sure every choice feels motivated and alive.\\n\\nIf you’d like me to take a look at your short script, I’ll send you detailed notes, a summary of overall impressions, and we can schedule a 30-minute call to talk through your piece. All I ask in return is an honest review of my consulting work — what helped, what didn’t, and how the experience felt.\\n\\nI’m only taking a few for now (3–5 scripts max), so if you’re interested, comment below or DM me a bit about your project!\\n\\n## Comments:\\n\\n- Comment nnfs08j: For the record, I think there are a lot of starting out writers who could use this leg up. I hope you get some bites.'}, {'id': '1olhxoz', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1olhxoz: Cinema with a Cause | Film #1 — “Nero’s guests” - the documentary that turned inequality into a moral indictment\\n\\n\\n\\n## Comments:'}, {'id': '1ova2ba', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1ova2ba: Crocodile Dance Teaser (Africanfuturist Feature in Development)\\n\\n\\n\\n## Comments:'}, {'id': '1oryipz', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1oryipz: How Humans in the Loop Turns AI Jargon into Social Critique\\n\\n\\n\\n## Comments:'}, {'id': '1omdy0f', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1omdy0f: My Student Film Final - Into The Mainframe\\n\\n\\n\\n## Comments:'}, {'id': '1otv4qs', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1otv4qs: Virtual Test Screening\\n\\nHey guys, looking for a small focus group for a new dark pop series trailer I’ve been working on. Would love feedback during the screening. Very short, between 15-20 minutes. Totally free but limited. Sign up is below!\\n\\nSign Up:\\n\\n## Comments:'}, {'id': '1omsgqf', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1omsgqf: Hidden War: The Real Truth Beyond Sound of Freedom\\n\\n\\n\\n## Comments:'}, {'id': '1ou20pq', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1ou20pq: DLSU MARKETING RESEARCH SURVEY\\n\\n\\n\\n## Comments:'}, {'id': '1opiu8f', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1opiu8f: \"Film this!\" on Tubi - Filming a film and filming a film being filmed. It\\'s a lot F\\'s but it works out in the end.\\n\\nIndie Portuguese movie made on a shoestring budget but with a lot of heart.   \\n  \\nTwo filmmakers must set aside their history to film a crucial scene. Egos clash and tensions rise as everything unravels before day\\'s end. A film that could only have been made once, shot sequentially, without takes, always in character.\\n\\nIt\\'s shot in a mockumentary-style, mainly from the POV of the BTS cam.\\n\\nTo add to the chaos everyone had a different scripts and secret instructions; it was definitely a unique experience.\\n\\n  \\n**TUBI:** [**\\n\\n**RELAY:** [**\\n\\n## Comments:'}, {'id': '1oo6kn3', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1oo6kn3: Perariyathavar (2013): When Silence Becomes Protest\\n\\n\\n\\n## Comments:'}, {'id': '1om7w0u', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1om7w0u: Welcome to the The HourBack Creator’s Code — 5-Part Series…Part 1…(questions from audience)\\n\\n\\n\\n## Comments:'}, {'id': '1orziog', 'markdown_content': \"# Post 1orziog: New Filmmakers Looking For Critique on Atmosphere\\n\\n**TLDR: We're new filmmakers (a production team of two) looking for feedback/critique on how well we used technical elements like lighting, camera, editing to create mood and atmosphere, and where we can improve for Season 2.**\\n\\nHi Guys!\\n\\nWe’re new filmmakers and a production crew made up entirely of two friends that handled everything on this project: writing, sound, lighting, directing, editing, etc. This was mostly because we wanted to force ourselves to learn how to do everything first and be better equipped to communicate wants and needs to crew down the road once we’re ready to expand our team and tackle more ambitious\\xa0projects. This definitely led to some headaches, but ultimately we're happy we did it as we learned A LOT along the way. Especially when it came to editing...Wow...I have SO MUCH MORE RESPECT for editors after all of this and I say that as someone who already felt they essentially rewrite the movie and craft a lot of an actor’s performance and don’t get enough credit for such. I digress.\\n\\nOver the last 7–8 months, we made a six-episode anthology series on YouTube inspired by The Twilight Zone and Black Mirror. You can (hopefully) see us grow from episode to episode, but we’re sharing our final episode since it best reflects what we learned along the way.\\n\\nFor this episode, we pushed ourselves technically — experimenting with lighting, camera work, and practical effects to create a haunted-house vibe (something in the vein of The Conjuring, but with some humor mixed in). It’s also our first episode featuring more than just the two of us on screen.\\n\\nTo be honest, we didn’t give ourselves the best schedule to reflect on things between each episode we filmed, but we’re taking the time now before embarking on a season 2 to gather feedback and critiques and hopefully identify areas to improve and some areas that we succeeded in, but can maybe expand on.\\xa0\\n\\nWe'd really appreciate any and all honest feedback: good, bad, harsh, etc.\\xa0— especially on how we used technical elements (camera, lighting, editing) to create mood and atmosphere. We're trying to learn as much as we can as fast as we can so that we can make cooler stuff that better resembles what we have in our\\xa0heads and better entertain everyone.\\xa0\\n\\nThanks so much for taking the time!!\\n\\n## Comments:\"}, {'id': '1oo2lgc', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1oo2lgc: Filmmaking as gesture, not spectacle\\n\\nIn this week’s issue from\\xa0**Veili**, a collective platform and journal for independent filmmakers, we look at how craft can process what can’t be neatly resolved.\\n\\n•\\xa0*A Moment of Innocence*\\xa0and the ethics of reenactment as self-portrait  \\n• A Gabonese student doc that listens instead of explaining  \\n• A handmade Frankenstein short built from watercolor, paper, and a puppet  \\n• Notes from\\xa0Shelby Oaks\\xa0on designing fear through planning, not chaos\\n\\nIt’s about the overlap between craft, tenderness and precision, where image-making becomes a way of thinking.  \\n  \\nWould love to hear how these approaches connect with your own work.\\n\\nRead it here: [The Gesture That Remains](\\n\\n## Comments:'}, {'id': '1oxu1i0', 'markdown_content': \"# Post 1oxu1i0: Teaser: TRUTH! A surrealist vision\\n\\nHey, filmmakers and enthusiasts! My teaser is now on YouTube and I could use some help getting the views up...\\n\\nTRUTH! (2025) is a psychological, non-linear microshort that explores cis, male repression and memory fragmentation. I did everything by myself :). \\n\\nIt's 10 seconds long. Thank you for the support.\\n\\n## Comments:\"}, {'id': '1ot85po', 'markdown_content': '# Post 1ot85po: Teaser for #theyellowlighter\\n\\nThe dream was never hers alone—something else was dreaming back.#theyellowlighter #quantumentanglement\\n\\n## Comments:'}]\n\nUSER QUERY:\nWhat are some themes in these conversations\n\nINSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Answer the user's query based ONLY on the information provided in the context.\n2. If the user's query is not related to the context, say \"I don't have enough information to answer this question.\"\n3. If the context doesn't contain enough information to answer the query, say \"I don't have enough information to answer this question.\"\n4. Do not make up information or use knowledge outside of the provided context.\n5. For every piece of evidence you cite, add a reference at the end of the sentence in the format [postID] where postID is the exact ID of the source document.\n6. Example of proper reference: \"Users are experiencing battery life issues with the device [qpmkvr].\"\n7. Make sure all postID references are accurate and correspond to actual post IDs from the provided context.\n8. Do not modify the postID format - keep it exactly as shown in the context (do not add extra characters or modify the ID).\n9. Organize your response using markdown section headers (##) to categorize different perspectives.\n10. Use headers like \"## Positive Perspectives\", \"## Criticisms\", \"## Feature Requests\", \"## Common Issues\", etc. as appropriate for the query.\n11. Under each section header, provide a bulleted list explaining the key points with references.\n\n\nANSWER:\n"